" data-explanation="" data-pick="6" data-side="1"><title>Audit each product — Prove the harm for the specific part being taxed.</title><path data-hit="" d="M577 825h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="585" y="855" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Audit each product</text><text x="911" y="855" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#634381" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">57.5</text><rect x="881" y="862" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="881" y="862" width="34.5" height="5" rx="2" fill="#634381"/><text x="1006" y="855" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#18</text><text x="585" y="886" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >Prove the harm for the specific part being</text><text x="585" y="906" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >taxed.</text></g><rect x="36" y="908" width="1008" height="1" rx="0" fill="#cad3ca"/><rect x="36" y="909" width="1008" height="83" rx="0" fill="#eff1e9"/><text x="68" y="958" font-size="35" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle">7</text><g data-argument-id="person-047-07" data-reader-id="person-047-07" data-rank="16" data-impact="67.5" data-author="Júlia Nunes" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="7" data-side="0"><title>Count the local shops — One factory buys gauges, repairs and transport nearby.</title><path data-hit="" d="M108 909h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="116" y="939" font-size="25" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Count the local shops</text><text x="442" y="939" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#245d40" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">67.5</text><rect x="412" y="946" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="412" y="946" width="40.5" height="5" rx="2" fill="#245d40"/><text x="537" y="939" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#16</text><text x="116" y="970" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >One factory buys gauges, repairs and</text><text x="116" y="990" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >transport nearby.</text></g><g data-argument-id="person-165-07" data-reader-id="person-165-07" data-rank="9" data-impact="75" data-author="Temilade Afolayan" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="7" data-side="1"><title>Keep bids competitive — A protected supplier has less reason to cut its price.</title><path data-hit="" d="M577 909h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="585" y="939" font-size="25" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Keep bids competitive</text><text x="911" y="939" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#634381" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">75</text><rect x="881" y="946" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="881" y="946" width="45" height="5" rx="2" fill="#634381"/><text x="1006" y="939" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#9</text><text x="585" y="970" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >A protected supplier has less reason to cut its</text><text x="585" y="990" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >price.</text></g><rect x="36" y="992" width="1008" height="1" rx="0" fill="#cad3ca"/><text x="68" y="1042" font-size="35" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle">8</text><g data-argument-id="person-047-08" data-reader-id="person-047-08" data-rank="14" data-impact="70" data-author="Júlia Nunes" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="8" data-side="0"><title>Win a concession — Offer to lift a duty when the subsidy ends.</title><path data-hit="" d="M108 993h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="116" y="1023" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Win a concession</text><text x="442" y="1023" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#245d40" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">70</text><rect x="412" y="1030" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="412" y="1030" width="42" height="5" rx="2" fill="#245d40"/><text x="537" y="1023" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#14</text><text x="116" y="1054" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >Offer to lift a duty when the subsidy ends.</text></g><g data-argument-id="person-165-08" data-reader-id="person-165-08" data-rank="19" data-impact="57.5" data-author="Temilade Afolayan" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="8" data-side="1"><title>Price the paperwork — Small orders still need classification and origin checks.</title><path data-hit="" d="M577 993h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="585" y="1023" font-size="25" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Price the paperwork</text><text x="911" y="1023" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#634381" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">57.5</text><rect x="881" y="1030" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="881" y="1030" width="34.5" height="5" rx="2" fill="#634381"/><text x="1006" y="1023" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#19</text><text x="585" y="1054" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >Small orders still need classification and</text><text x="585" y="1074" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >origin checks.</text></g><rect x="36" y="1076" width="1008" height="1" rx="0" fill="#cad3ca"/><rect x="36" y="1077" width="1008" height="83" rx="0" fill="#eff1e9"/><text x="68" y="1126" font-size="35" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle">9</text><g data-argument-id="person-047-09" data-reader-id="person-047-09" data-rank="7" data-impact="80" data-author="Júlia Nunes" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="9" data-side="0"><title>Protect scarce inputs — Start with parts that cannot be replaced quickly.</title><path data-hit="" d="M108 1077h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="116" y="1107" font-size="25" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Protect scarce inputs</text><text x="442" y="1107" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#245d40" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">80</text><rect x="412" y="1114" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="412" y="1114" width="48" height="5" rx="2" fill="#245d40"/><text x="537" y="1107" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#7</text><text x="116" y="1138" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >Start with parts that cannot be replaced</text><text x="116" y="1158" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >quickly.</text></g><g data-argument-id="person-165-09" data-reader-id="person-165-09" data-rank="12" data-impact="72.5" data-author="Temilade Afolayan" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="9" data-side="1"><title>Fund the bottleneck — Spend directly on training or tooling where it is scarce.</title><path data-hit="" d="M577 1077h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="585" y="1107" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Fund the bottleneck</text><text x="911" y="1107" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#634381" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">72.5</text><rect x="881" y="1114" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="881" y="1114" width="43.5" height="5" rx="2" fill="#634381"/><text x="1006" y="1107" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#12</text><text x="585" y="1138" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >Spend directly on training or tooling where it is</text><text x="585" y="1158" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >scarce.</text></g><rect x="36" y="1160" width="1008" height="1" rx="0" fill="#cad3ca"/><text x="68" y="1210" font-size="35" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle">10</text><g data-argument-id="person-047-10" data-reader-id="person-047-10" data-rank="20" data-impact="57.5" data-author="Júlia Nunes" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="10" data-side="0"><title>Make firms earn it — Renew duties only if factories invest and deliver.</title><path data-hit="" d="M108 1161h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="116" y="1191" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Make firms earn it</text><text x="442" y="1191" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#245d40" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">57.5</text><rect x="412" y="1198" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="412" y="1198" width="34.5" height="5" rx="2" fill="#245d40"/><text x="537" y="1191" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#20</text><text x="116" y="1222" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >Renew duties only if factories invest and</text><text x="116" y="1242" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >deliver.</text></g><g data-argument-id="person-165-10" data-reader-id="person-165-10" data-rank="17" data-impact="62.5" data-author="Temilade Afolayan" data-confidence="" data-explanation="" data-pick="10" data-side="1"><title>Make the exit real — Customers need a firm date to compare long-term bids.</title><path data-hit="" d="M577 1161h464v83h-464z" fill="transparent"/><text x="585" y="1191" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" >Make the exit real</text><text x="911" y="1191" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#634381" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="impact">62.5</text><rect x="881" y="1198" width="60" height="5" rx="2" fill="#d5dcd5"/><rect x="881" y="1198" width="37.5" height="5" rx="2" fill="#634381"/><text x="1006" y="1191" font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#142d21" text-anchor="middle" data-metric="rank">#17</text><text x="585" y="1222" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >Customers need a firm date to compare</text><text x="585" y="1242" font-size="19" font-weight="400" fill="#40594b" >long-term bids.</text></g><rect x="36" y="1244" width="1008" height="1" rx="0" fill="#cad3ca"/><rect x="0" y="1260" width="1080" height="90" rx="0" fill="#172e23"/><text x="36" y="1296" font-size="24" font-weight="700" fill="#f5f7ee" data-activity="">Editorial scenario · Nov. 26, 2026</text><text x="1044" y="1296" font-size="24" font-weight="700" fill="#d6efdc" text-anchor="end">differkindly.com</text><text x="36" y="1328" font-size="20" font-weight="400" fill="#d8e6dc" data-rubric="">Differ Impact = 50% magnitude + 30% reach + 20% duration. Highest impact ranks first.</text></svg>',now());

insert into dk_editorial.poster_authors(slug,persona) values ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047'),('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165');

insert into dk_safety.points(slug,id,side,rank,impact_rank,title,detail,sources,counterpoint) values
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-01','Raise targeted tariffs',1,4,'Keep the line running','If a supplier closes, you can buy the machines at auction. You can’t buy the crew back that way. I’d use a duty where a subsidy threatens an otherwise viable line.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'An American factory can pay a duty on a component before it sells the finished machine. Count those costs when you tell me how many jobs this saves.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-02','Raise targeted tariffs',2,2,'Keep a second source','Before we let the last domestic source go, price out a week with no usable parts. Keeping a second qualified supplier has value even when its bid is higher.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'A cheap substitute is no bargain if it doesn’t fit the unit. Give me a qualified part and a delivery date before you make the existing part more expensive.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-03','Raise targeted tariffs',3,8,'Price the subsidy','Show me the actual subsidy and the cost advantage it creates. If those explain why a capable U.S. plant loses the bid, a targeted duty makes sense.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'I’d look at a case involving a specific subsidized product. A long list of trading partners tells me very little about the part number on my bench.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-04','Raise targeted tariffs',4,10,'Give tooling time','Nobody tools up for one purchase order. A defined period of protection could give customers time to sign orders that pay for a new die.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'If a lack of trained machinists is the problem, price a training contract. Compare the cost per qualified worker with the cost of taxing every buyer.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-05','Raise targeted tariffs',5,11,'Train the next crew','A trainee learns a defect by seeing one on the line. If every shift is at risk of cancellation, who’s going to train the next quality lead?','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'If a lack of trained machinists is the problem, price a training contract. Compare the cost per qualified worker with the cost of taxing every buyer.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-06','Raise targeted tariffs',6,15,'Hold wage gains','If one of two big employers disappears, switching jobs gets a lot harder. I’d count wages and retention when we review whether a duty worked.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'When a walk-in cooler quits, somebody has to pay for the compressor. If there’s no domestic replacement on the shelf, the duty just makes that repair cost more.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-07','Raise targeted tariffs',7,16,'Count the local shops','I want the review to include the little shops that calibrate gauges and repair our tools. Their order books move when a larger plant cuts shifts.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'An American factory can pay a duty on a component before it sells the finished machine. Count those costs when you tell me how many jobs this saves.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-08','Raise targeted tariffs',8,14,'Win a concession','Give the trading partner a way out. Name the subsidy, spell out how we would verify its removal, and lift the duty when that happens.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'Our customers aren’t all in the United States. If buyers abroad face new duties in response, a factory that never asked for protection can lose orders.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-09','Raise targeted tariffs',9,7,'Protect scarce inputs','We should know which parts take months to qualify. If there’s no domestic capacity to save or rebuild, putting a duty on my parts list makes little sense.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'A cheap substitute is no bargain if it doesn’t fit the unit. Give me a qualified part and a delivery date before you make the existing part more expensive.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-047-10','Raise targeted tariffs',10,20,'Make firms earn it','Set a review date. If the protected company raises prices but doesn’t add capacity, qualify another line or train workers, let the duty expire.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'A temporary duty can outlast the problem. Show me who has authority to end it and what evidence buyers can bring to that review.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-01','Reject the proposed hikes',11,5,'The repair bill','When a walk-in cooler quits, somebody has to pay for the compressor. If there’s no domestic replacement on the shelf, the duty just makes that repair cost more.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'We should know which parts take months to qualify. If there’s no domestic capacity to save or rebuild, putting a duty on my parts list makes little sense.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-02','Reject the proposed hikes',12,1,'Factories buy parts','An American factory can pay a duty on a component before it sells the finished machine. Count those costs when you tell me how many jobs this saves.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'I want the review to include the little shops that calibrate gauges and repair our tools. Their order books move when a larger plant cuts shifts.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-03','Reject the proposed hikes',13,6,'Keep spares available','A cheap substitute is no bargain if it doesn’t fit the unit. Give me a qualified part and a delivery date before you make the existing part more expensive.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'Before we let the last domestic source go, price out a week with no usable parts. Keeping a second qualified supplier has value even when its bid is higher.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-04','Reject the proposed hikes',14,13,'Protect small shops','The importer pays first. If that cost shows up on my supplier invoice, I finance it while I’m waiting for the customer to pay me.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'Nobody tools up for one purchase order. A defined period of protection could give customers time to sign orders that pay for a new die.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-05','Reject the proposed hikes',15,3,'Count export losses','Our customers aren’t all in the United States. If buyers abroad face new duties in response, a factory that never asked for protection can lose orders.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'Give the trading partner a way out. Name the subsidy, spell out how we would verify its removal, and lift the duty when that happens.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-06','Reject the proposed hikes',16,18,'Audit each product','I’d look at a case involving a specific subsidized product. A long list of trading partners tells me very little about the part number on my bench.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'Show me the actual subsidy and the cost advantage it creates. If those explain why a capable U.S. plant loses the bid, a targeted duty makes sense.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-07','Reject the proposed hikes',17,9,'Keep bids competitive','Even a domestic supplier can raise its bid when the imported alternative gets more expensive. Check actual quotes after the duty takes effect.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'Set a review date. If the protected company raises prices but doesn’t add capacity, qualify another line or train workers, let the duty expire.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-08','Reject the proposed hikes',18,19,'Price the paperwork','A shop ordering one valve can face the same classification question as a chain ordering a thousand. Figure staff time and brokerage into the cost.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'We should know which parts take months to qualify. If there’s no domestic capacity to save or rebuild, putting a duty on my parts list makes little sense.'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-09','Reject the proposed hikes',19,12,'Fund the bottleneck','If a lack of trained machinists is the problem, price a training contract. Compare the cost per qualified worker with the cost of taxing every buyer.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'A trainee learns a defect by seeing one on the line. If every shift is at risk of cancellation, who’s going to train the next quality lead?'),
  ('tariffs-on-subsidized-imports','person-165-10','Reject the proposed hikes',20,17,'Make the exit real','A temporary duty can outlast the problem. Show me who has authority to end it and what evidence buyers can bring to that review.','["https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2026/november/ustr-makes-determinations-and-proposes-actions-14-section-301-investigations-relating-structural", "https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/pub5405.pdf"]'::jsonb,'Set a review date. If the protected company raises prices but doesn’t add capacity, qualify another line or train workers, let the duty expire.');

